\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{Refining a triangle}
\date{2026-11-06}

\p{The cycle sum uses two paths between one pair of vertices. A
triangle admits a different elimination. Place a midpoint on
each of its three edges and join the midpoints, producing 9
edges on 6 vertices. Eliminating the midpoints leaves a
quadratic form on the three corners. Repeating the
construction produces a graph at every level. Which factor
converts the refined graph into the quadratic form on the
previous vertices?}
